      "writtenOn": "2026-03-18T04:48:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe `__GFP_KSWAPD_RECLAIM` is actually a better choice here.  The thing is this is zs_pool allocation, which is a long-living allocation: we potentially take pages out of emergency pools for a long time. I assume most (if not all) `GFP_ATOMIC` allocations are short-lived, which makes sense. But zs_pool is a different story. Maybe we need to keep it out of `__GFP_HIGH` pools.",
      "parentUuid": "a06e38c2_80c42c3a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1045,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 1045,
        "endChar": 19
